            <physDesc xml:id="physDesc_931cea38">
               <titlePage label="Title page" xml:id="titlePage_48cf5039">
                  <p xml:id="idm32">Der Taucher / von Schiller / als Melodrama componiert / und Herrn Professor Nielsen gewidmet / von I:P:E: Hartmann. / Op: 21.</p>
               </titlePage>
               <extent xml:id="extent_b2d305a1">75 pages</extent>
               <dimensions unit="cm" xml:id="dimensions_ab20af52">23.5 x 31</dimensions>
               <physMedium xml:id="physMedium_4bd86980">In blue cardboard cover with cloth spine. Handwritten label pasted on front cover inscribed:" CL A; IV <rend xml:id="idm36" rend="sup">
                     <rend xml:id="idm37" rend="underline">a</rend>
                  </rend> / H 2 P.3. I.P.E. Hartmann / Der Taucher / Ballade von Fr. Schiller / Melodram / op 21 / Partitur.". On the inside of the cover in Hartmann's hand: "1<rend xml:id="idm38" rend="sup">ste</rend> gang fremsagt i Hr. Instructeur Nielsens Aftenunderholdning 1837. 2<rend xml:id="idm39" rend="sup">den</rend> [Gang] i Frimurer Localet til Hr. Kølles [Aftenunderholdning] [1837] 3<rend xml:id="idm40" rend="sup">die</rend> [Gang] i Blinde Institutets [Aftenunderholdning] 10/2 1838. 4<rend xml:id="idm41" rend="sup">de</rend> [Gang] i Kellermanns Aftenunderholdning 10/3 1839. 5<rend xml:id="idm42" rend="sup">te</rend> [Gang] i Musikforeningens Concert 1855. 6<rend xml:id="idm43" rend="sup">te</rend> [Gang] i Linckes Concert Marts 56." Enclosed Danish translation of Schiller's text by Edvard Lembcke, dated "11/2 84". Written in brown ink. Paper: 14 staves. Paginated 1-75 in Hartmann's hand. At the end of the music on p. 75 dated "d: 25/3 37."</physMedium>
            </physDesc>
